# Art: finished drawings from the shelf, named by what they are. `draw` is one line of intent; the server puts the figure's parts on stage
# as ordinary shapes (fox1-tail, kid1-hair), so a label can point at a part and the whole figure can move. pnpm check plays it through
# the server's line path (it needs a shelf), so the parts, the label and the placeholder for an okapi are looked for on screen. A callout carries a leader to its part, so wherever
# the painter puts the word it still points at the tail; the placeholder is named, so nobody wonders what the grey shape is.

look paper
scene shelf figure canvas=square lines=2
draw fox1 fox at=27,34 size=46 | sitting, facing left
draw kid1 child at=76,34 size=46 | standing
draw fox2 fox at=27,78 size=30 new | sitting, facing right
draw okapi1 okapi at=76,70 size=34
say callout near=fox1-tail | tail
say label near=okapi1:below | okapi: not on the shelf yet
say | A fox, a child and a smaller fox facing the other way, each drawn from the shelf by name.
wait 1.5s
say | A figure is one thing: this line moves the whole child.
move kid1 66,34 over=1s
wait 2
